    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY. It does not say Rat.inv satisfies a law on the NEGATIVES: the hypothesis is 0 < q, and the negative branch is deliberately unproved (inv q = -(inv (-q)) recovers it in one case split when something needs it). It does not say \u211a's order is decidable as a Bool -- Rat.le_or_lt is a Prop-valued Or, and no Bool-valued comparator exists here. It does not say anything about \u211d: CReal has no inverse, and CReal.no_total_inverse proves that no total one can exist.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
